WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.918
Welcome to Grade 1 English, Unit 1: Welcome to School.

2
00:00:03.998 --> 00:00:09.323
You will learn the words for things
in your classroom, some colour words,

3
00:00:09.403 --> 00:00:12.950
and how to say your own name and how old you are.

4
00:00:13.030 --> 00:00:18.799
School is a happy, welcoming place, and
this unit helps you feel at home in it.

5
00:00:18.879 --> 00:00:26.573
Say the words out loud and enjoy them — this is about
brave first steps in English, not perfect spelling.

6
00:00:26.653 --> 00:00:32.792
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

7
00:00:32.872 --> 00:00:40.895
By the end of this unit, you will be able to name
common classroom objects (table, chair, book, pencil…)

8
00:00:40.975 --> 00:00:46.115
You will also name and point to
colours (red, blue, green, yellow…)

9
00:00:46.195 --> 00:00:48.764
You will also say “My name is ___.

10
00:00:48.844 --> 00:00:50.245
I am ___ years old.

11
00:00:50.325 --> 00:00:51.180
I like ___.”

12
00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:54.063
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

13
00:00:54.143 --> 00:00:59.904
Your vocabulary work begins with these words:
table, chair, whiteboard, ABC chart, clock, book.

14
00:00:59.984 --> 00:01:04.885
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

15
00:01:04.965 --> 00:01:08.758
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

16
00:01:08.838 --> 00:01:13.372
The reading sequence includes Amal's
First Day and Talk about Welcome to School.

17
00:01:13.452 --> 00:01:14.179
Read actively.

18
00:01:14.259 --> 00:01:18.159
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

19
00:01:18.239 --> 00:01:21.907
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

20
00:01:21.987 --> 00:01:25.939
The first language focus is Name a thing in your classroom.

21
00:01:26.019 --> 00:01:28.740
Hold up one classroom object and name it.

22
00:01:28.820 --> 00:01:33.796
Say 'a' before most words, but 'an'
before a vowel sound: a pen, an apple.

23
00:01:33.876 --> 00:01:41.244
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

24
00:01:41.324 --> 00:01:45.108
In speaking, you will complete Speaking 1 - Listen and point.

25
00:01:45.188 --> 00:01:49.352
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

26
00:01:49.432 --> 00:01:52.582
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

27
00:01:52.662 --> 00:01:55.940
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

28
00:01:56.020 --> 00:01:57.459
You are ready to begin.

29
00:01:57.539 --> 00:02:03.999
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

30
00:02:04.079 --> 00:02:07.170
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

31
00:02:07.250 --> 00:02:14.503
Use AI English for hints and feedback any time, and bring
your questions to a live session too if you join one.
